// Block prototypes (work items 0005, 0006 and 0008). The first entry must be
// air: its dense index is 0, the value every new chunk is filled with.
// A block that is not solid (water, torch) is drawn where it touches a
// different block that is not solid, and solid blocks show their faces
// against it. Water shows against other water only where the other
// surface is lower.
// hardness_seconds is the time to break the block by hand. 0 means the
// block cannot be mined (air, water).
// texture holds one base colour (red, green, blue) per face group. The atlas
// generator turns each into a 16 by 16 tile with a little per texel noise.
// Solid blocks are opaque to light, every other block lets light through.
// light_level (0 to 15, default 0) is the block light the block emits.
// water_level (default 0) marks water: 8 is a source block, 7 to 1 are
// flowing water, 7 next to a source and 1 at the far end of a spread.
// Water needs one block for every level from 1 to 8 or none at all.
